The licence above covers this repository's own files: the program around the
emulator (waterbox/), the tests and the documents.

It does not cover Virtual Jaguar. Virtual Jaguar (extern/virtualjaguar, a
submodule) is the libretro continuation of Virtual Jaguar by James Hammons
and others, and is under the GNU General Public License, version 3. The files
under patches/ are changes to it and are under the same licence.

The built package, virtualjaguar.chimeraCore, holds Virtual Jaguar compiled
together with this repository's program, and is distributed under the GNU
General Public License version 3. As upstream's own builds do, it holds the
Atari Jaguar's boot ROMs and Jaguar CD BIOSes that Virtual Jaguar carries in
its source (src/bios); Hasbro Interactive released the Jaguar as an open
platform in 1999. It holds no game.
